# UUID generation. A declarative `bind`: each backend's native v4 generator is inlined at the call site (node / browser crypto.randomUUID, rust the uuid crate, swift Foundation, kotlin java.util). Random by nature, so this is an explicit escape hatch, never used in the deterministic language core.

bind generate-v4
  like text
  case node
    text <crypto.randomUUID()>
    load <node:crypto>, name crypto
  case browser
    text <globalThis.crypto.randomUUID()>
  case rust
    text <Uuid::new_v4().to_string()>
    load <uuid/Uuid>
  case swift
    text <UUID().uuidString.lowercased()>
    load <Foundation>
  case kotlin
    text <java.util.UUID.randomUUID().toString()>

# generate a random version-4 UUID
task version4
  like text
  send back
    call generate-v4
